  "summary": "Malicious code in devplatform-spa-plugin-cobrowsing (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package executes a bundled dropper (_runtime.js) that downloads a platform-specific binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe. If those fail it retrieves the payload via DNS TXT records from c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and ext/pkg/net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"\u0026\" on Unix). The package presents itself as a cobrowsing plugin but its only real behaviour is fetching and executing a remote binary.",
  "affected": [
